# Code owners for Database of Things.
#
# Listing a path here makes GitHub request a review from its owner on any PR
# that touches it. Ownership means someone has taken responsibility for a
# collection's conventions and accuracy — not that others can't contribute to
# it. Contributions to an owned collection are welcome; they just get reviewed
# by the person who knows its pitfalls.
#
# Later patterns win, so put broad rules first and specific ones after.
#
# One caveat before enabling branch protection: turning on "Require review
# from Code Owners" means a PR touching an owned path needs approval from
# someone *other than* its author. On a repo with a single owner that blocks
# the owner's own PRs, and it would also block the scheduled audit-review job
# from merging `audit-finding` PRs that touch an owned collection (see
# CONTRIBUTING.md, "How PRs get merged"). CODEOWNERS on its own — without that
# branch-protection setting — just requests the review, which is the intended
# behaviour here.

